      "normalized_sha256": "dbfc0d4c3175b4500c8cf75aa233cec5e0c9c3cee743890140512a0182f4cafa",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded base equation of the factorAcc mathematical summary: when the remaining value is below the candidate divisor, it defines the summary result to be the accumulated sequence.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-dbfc0d4c3175b4500c8cf75aa233cec5e0c9c3cee743890140512a0182f4cafa",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule factorAcc(A:ValSeq, N:Int, D:Int) => A\n    requires N <Int D"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 18,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "a835c97bf031675f196bffdf44a60757b87fcba3d1c37ef34f793bef42ba0e65",
      "rationale": "This is the divisible-case recurrence defining factorAcc by appending the current divisor, replacing the remaining value by the supplied-semantics quotient, and recurring at the same divisor.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-a835c97bf031675f196bffdf44a60757b87fcba3d1c37ef34f793bef42ba0e65",
      "start_line": 13,
      "text": "  rule factorAcc(A:ValSeq, N:Int, D:Int)\n    => factorAcc(\n         valSeqConcat(A, vCons(D, .ValSeq)),\n         (N -Int pyMod(N, D)) /Int D,\n         D)\n    requires D <=Int N andBool pyMod(N, D) ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 22,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "5fab523961a49385350dd07993fa3e83246b724eb1f40138964ce039d42a8f55",
      "rationale": "This is the non-divisible-case recurrence defining factorAcc by advancing the candidate divisor while preserving the accumulator and remaining value.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-5fab523961a49385350dd07993fa3e83246b724eb1f40138964ce039d42a8f55",
      "start_line": 20,
      "text": "  rule factorAcc(A:ValSeq, N:Int, D:Int)\n    => factorAcc(A, N, D +Int 1)\n    requires D <=Int N andBool pyMod(N, D) =/=Int 0"
    }
  ],
